    "created_at": "2026-11-13T20:57:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T20:57:37Z",
    "body": "Field evidence for Phases 2 and 3 from a real two-sided job: a small part with HAT-style stock and soft jaws (user's project), with the CamCraft **v0.19.0** release CLI, driven headlessly over MCP.\n\n**The part:**\n- a 30 mm cube made of two L-shaped halves, giving one 15 mm quadrant step from each side;\n- every edge filleted R3.125 mm.\n\n**The setups:**\n- Setup 1 machines the top.\n- Setup 2 flips the part about X (part alignment) on \"what Setup 1 leaves behind\", to machine the bottom step and its fillets.\n\n**What v0.19.0 refuses in Setup 2:**\n- `setup 'Setup 2' holds the part turned (part alignment) - 3D Pocket is not supported yet in an aligned setup (Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive are)`.\n- Picks (faces and edges) and area controls in the aligned setup are refused too.\n\n**The effect for the user:**\n- The bottom-side 3D work cannot be programmed at all: the bottom fillets and the fillets on the bottom notch's floor. Only face-off and a 2D adaptive of the notch are possible, and those 3D features stay unmachined.\n- The only workaround is to re-import the part pre-rotated as a separate model in its own unaligned setup. That loses the carried stock.\n\n**The kinds this job needs**, as a data point for Phase 3's kind-by-kind order: 3D Pocket (roughing the bottom notch with a 6.35 mm flat end mill) and a 3D finish over the fillets. Picks are needed for 2D Contour and 2D Pocket on the flipped side.\n\n(Filed as a comment rather than a new issue, because this issue's Phases 2 and 3 cover it.)\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
